gst-gtk-dovi-map (0.1.0+rogdv12) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Diagnostics only; rendering, return values, retries and fallbacks are
    unchanged.
  * Forward libplacebo and Dolby provider messages to the gtkdovimap debug
    category: one process-wide pl_log, created before the first device and
    never destroyed, is given to the Vulkan device, shader cache, dispatch,
    renderer and provider. Its level follows the category threshold.
  * Name the failing step in the frame render error instead of the bare
    "Eligible Dolby frame normalization/mapping failed", for every exit
    that set no reason, including the provider transport pass.

 -- ROG HDR contributors <rog-hdr@invalid>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000

gst-gtk-dovi-map (0.1.0+rogdv11) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Let the renderer decide whether a Profile 7 master is reconstructed.
    Upload the enhancement layer only for an active NLQ, the only case the
    renderer samples it, instead of declining every Profile 7 picture
    without one. A Profile 7 MEL (identity NLQ, zero residual) now reaches
    the provider as a complete master; FEL and single-layer pictures are
    unchanged.
  * Depend on and build against libplacebo-rog387 1.0.0+private20261108-3
    or later, which decides a zero residual from the raw RPU. An older
    renderer would make every MEL picture render twice (a declined Dolby
    pass, then the baseline) and never map it.
  * Name the decline when the renderer reports the master not reconstructed.

 -- ROG HDR contributors <rog-hdr@invalid>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:45:00 +0000

gst-gtk-dovi-map (0.1.0+rogdv10) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Accept each native input domain with the overlay composition meta too,
    paired with a graded output that declares it, so a subtitle overlay in
    front of the mapper attaches its overlays instead of downloading and
    blending them into the pictures.
  * Destroy Vulkan devices on a thread of this library: unloading the NVIDIA
    driver releases the calling thread's current EGL context, which crashed
    WebKit's tile painter after a source change.

 -- ROG HDR contributors <rog-hdr@invalid>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:30:00 +0000

